      "notes": "Paper's FFCPS, FF6PS, SY and DHS columns are SKIPPED — Pastor-Stambaugh LIQ factor and Stambaugh-Yuan / DHS factor series are not available in the ClickHouse FF catalog (see data_verification.json). CAPM alpha is computed by definition as `ret - rf - beta*mkt_rf`; not separately encoded as a target because it equals FF3 alpha + 0 (CAPM is a sub-model of FF3) only when SMB/HML/MOM betas happen to be uncorrelated — here CAPM differs from FF3; replicating FF3, FFC4, FF5, FF6 suffices to test the multi-model alphas that are the paper's substantive claim. Decile spread (D10-D1) cells are signed (D10 minus D1)."
    },
    {
      "id": "T2",
      "table_ref": "Table 2",
      "description": "Time-series averages of cross-sectional medians of firm characteristics across MAX deciles",
      "replication_meaning": "Demonstrates that (i) MAX itself is computed correctly (monotonic 1.0% to 7.1% across deciles), (ii) the characteristic construction pipeline (BETA via 252-day rolling regression, IVOL from the same residuals, SIZE from CRSP, BM via SEQ+TXDB+ITCB-PSTKRV, REV as formation-month return, MOM as 11-month cumulative, ILLIQ via daily |ret|/dollar volume averaged monthly, I/A as annual asset growth, ROE as IBQ/quarter-lagged BE, CE as 12m log mcap growth minus 12m cumulative return) is consistent with the paper's formulas, and (iii) the decile sorts and cross-sectional-median aggregation yield the paper's monotone pattern. Downstream claim C3 (MAX-sorted portfolios are mispriced high-beta, high-IVOL, high-CE stocks held mostly by retail) depends on these characteristics being correctly constructed.",
      "covers_claims": ["C3"],
      "paper_quote": "Summary statistics for decile portfolios of stocks sorted by MAX: The reported values represent the time-series averages of the cross-sectional median values for the following firm-specific characteristics: MAX; market beta (BETA); the firm-level mispricing index of Stambaugh, Yu, and Yuan (2015) (MIS); composite equity issuance (CE), defined as the 12-month growth in equity market capitalization minus the 12-month cumulative stock return; the sensitivity of stock-level MAX to the market MAX estimated via 12-month rolling regressions (β^MAX); institutional holdings (INST); the expected idiosyncratic skewness measure of Boyer et al. (2010) (E(ISKEW)); market capitalization (SIZE); idiosyncratic volatility (IVOL); book-to-market ratio (BM); excess monthly return during the portfolio formation month (REV); intermediate-term momentum (MOM); Amihud (2002) illiquidity (ILLIQ); return on equity (ROE); and asset growth (I/A). The sample period spans April 1980 to December 2022 for INST and E(ISKEW), and January 1968 to December 2022 for all other characteristics.",
      "exercises_preprocessing_rules": ["var_max_definition", "var_beta_252d", "var_size", "var_book_equity", "var_bm", "var_mom", "var_rev", "var_illiq", "var_ia", "var_roe", "var_ivol", "var_ce_composite_equity_issuance", "sort_decile_max"],
